  "question_text": "What are Gestalt principles?",
  "generated_answer": "Gestalt principles are rules that explain how we organize sensory information into coherent, meaningful patterns. They include the figure‑ground relationship (distinguishing a focal object from its background), proximity (grouping nearby items), similarity (grouping alike items), the law of continuity (preferring smooth, continuous lines), and closure (tending to perceive complete shapes even when parts are missing). These principles help us interpret complex visual scenes by forming perceptual hypotheses based on past experience and expectations.",
